# Current model contracts

Resolve defaults and aliases before sanitizers. Defaults: DeepSeek `deepseek-flash`, MiMo `mimo-v2.6-pro`, GLM `glm-5.3`, Azure Claude `claude-sonnet-5-5`; Kimi `kimi-k3` and MiniMax `MiniMax-M3` stay unchanged. Compatible providers have only operator-configured defaults. Discovery remains entirely `CURSORPROXY_MODELS`; do not filter retired IDs or retarget old aliases.

- Native GLM-5.3/Flash/FlashX standard API requests validate low/high/max (default max), env > client > default, and always-on thinking. On native `/coding/` paths, GLM-5.3/Flash also accept none/minimal/medium/xhigh: forward them unchanged so upstream maps none/minimal/low to low, medium/high to high, and xhigh/max to max. None/minimal do not disable 5.3 thinking. `glmParameterError` is hostname-scoped; gateways and GLM-5.2 retain existing effort behavior. FlashX rejects Coding Plan endpoints. `GLM_NATIVE_FIELDS` still controls both sanitizer injection and cache-miss clear_thinking injection.
- DeepSeek Flash is multimodal; old Flash aliases are multimodal only on api.deepseek.com. V4 Pro stays bridged. `low` joins high/max; tool-bearing requests restore the full reasoning history. MiMo V2.6 Pro, Flash and Pro Ultraspeed are native image models; legacy V2.5 Pro stays bridged. Kimi K2.7 Code Highspeed shares the Code leaf rules. K3 keeps its intentional max policy.
- Fireworks IDs use canonical `deepseek-v4p1-flash`, `kimi-k3`, `glm-5p3`, `glm-5p3-flash`, `minimax-m3`. Bridge exact text-only GLM-5p3. Do not apply native Kimi/GLM sanitizers to hosted models. Keep the existing Fireworks GLM-5.2 override scoped to 5.2. TokenRouter discovery expansion is deferred pending authenticated evidence.
- MiniMax M3.1 Preview is opt-in, always adaptive, low/medium/high/xhigh/max (max default), and requires split reasoning. `lib/reasoning.js` wraps new string reasoning_content in a versioned internal cache envelope, concatenates stream deltas, and restores the original field. Legacy JSON reasoning_details entries remain readable and retain snapshot semantics. Never forward the internal envelope. M3.1 gets a model-qualified scope; legacy MiniMax scopes remain stable.
- GPT-6 capability handling lives in `lib/gpt.js`, runs after env/client effort resolution, and uses explicit published model names. Public OpenAI none/minimal normalization and Chat/tool restrictions apply only to api.openai.com. Azure none remains none. Sampling is removed unless effective effort is explicitly none. Cache-key effort normalization must match the outbound effective effort. Preserve `prompt_cache_options` and `cache_write_tokens`. Translate retention to options.ttl=30m only on the verified public endpoint; generic gateways and Azure keep their retention contract. No automatic wire-mode switch. Existing GPT-5.5/5.6 streaming/tool repairs remain narrow.
- New Claude IDs are exact Sonnet/Opus/Haiku 5.5 and Fable 5.1. All default to adaptive thinking; use `claudeThinkingActive` at every cache read/write gate. Adaptive accepts display; manual budgets are rejected. Sonnet between_tools accepts only type and low/medium/high effort. Only Haiku can disable thinking at <=high and supports forced tools. All accept xhigh; strip sampling only for new models. Preserve signature-only blocks.
- `claudeThinkingScope` isolates new models by provider, resolved model, upstream URL/account secret hash, system prompt, tools and proxy user. Both JSON and SSE use the same scope. Never log secret inputs or raw signatures. Legacy Claude scopes stay unchanged. Anthropic-compatible thinking caching remains opt-in.

Verification: `test/model-refresh.test.js` invokes the real handler with controlled fetch and KV. Test aliases/public/bare/provider routes, omitted defaults, native/gateway boundaries, JSON/SSE replay, original cache readability and isolation, tool bodies, errors without upstream calls, usage, image dispatch and explicit legacy discovery. Live quota/access and Cursor execution still require the manual matrix in `.cursor/test-cases/model-refresh.md`.

Primary contracts checked October 18, 2026: [DeepSeek thinking](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode), [MiMo thinking](https://mimo.mi.com/docs/en-US/quick-start/usage-guide/text-generation/deep-thinking), [GLM 5.3](https://docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-5.3), [Kimi models](https://platform.kimi.ai/docs/api/models-overview), [MiniMax Chat](https://platform.minimax.io/docs/api-reference/text-chat-openai), [GPT-6 migration](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model/gpt-6-astra#migration-quickstart), [Azure reasoning](https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/foundry/openai/how-to/reasoning), [Claude thinking](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/extended-thinking), [Fireworks quickstart](https://docs.fireworks.ai/getting-started/quickstart).
